  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureBotHT
    notes: Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 17603-42-8 present, but no CHEBI entry
      exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Curator can promote
      to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term.
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CHEBI via OLS (stem-substring)
    notes: Parent class identified via stem-substring; matched_via='DL-Glycerol 1-phosphate
      sodium salt hydrate'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:14336 (''glycerol 1-phosphate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:
      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'Catalogue line1378 names DL-glycerol1-phosphate sodium salt hydrate CAS17603-42-8.
      Inspected supplier61668 independently names the same racemic1-phosphate hydrate
      and CAS, but explicitly gives xNa+/yH2O. The phosphate position/racemic scope
      are supported; sodium and water stoichiometry must remain unspecified. The broader
      rac-glycerol1-phosphate parentCHEBI14336 is consistent. Retain CAS identity,
      use broadMatch, and do not equate with G6501 positional-isomer mixture. See
      the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/DL-Glycerol_1-phosphate_Sodium_Salt_Hydrate.yaml.
      Primary source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/14336/;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/17603-42-8/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON;
      https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/61668. Captures, exact input
      hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
